        "ballot_id": "B004",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of the distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages and their roles in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B001",
    "B016"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B004 identifies a foundational and enduring organizing principle of adaptive immunity. Miller and Cooper provide a focused, complementary attribution to the T- and B-cell lineages, respectively, and the biological framework has been confirmed and made consequential across immunology and medicine for decades.",
    "case_against": "The history of lymphocyte biology is extensive, so the boundary between the two defining lineage discoveries and later essential work requires careful historical delimitation. This is a reservation about allocation of credit, not about the maturity or importance of the central finding.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson places B001 first because chaperonin-assisted folding is a repeatedly confirmed fundamental mechanism with a particularly focused two-person attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B001 is exceptionally strong and that Horwich and Hartl form a coherent pair. I continue to place B004 ahead because the delineation of the two lymphocyte lineages supplied the cellular architecture of adaptive immunity itself, with an equally durable and unusually direct influence on both basic and clinical immunology."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg emphasizes the direct, mature cancer-prevention impact of HPV virus-like-particle vaccination in B016 and regards its three credited investigators as representing the core advance.",
        "response": "B016 is a compelling alternative with exceptional public-health significance. However, its attribution spans virology, vaccine design, and subsequent translation, whereas B004 more cleanly recognizes two complementary foundational discoveries whose central biological conclusion has long been settled."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann favors B009 because GLP-1 physiology has delivered major conceptual and therapeutic advances in diabetes and obesity.",
        "response": "The clinical impact of GLP-1 therapies is substantial, but the appropriate division between foundational peptide physiology and later drug-development contributions remains unresolved in the supplied evidence. B004 has a more sharply bounded achievement and attribution."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record supports treating Miller and Cooper alone as the most appropriate complete attribution for the stated two-lineage achievement."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
